    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      97.2,
      623.55,
      252.13,
      639.02
    ],
    "text": "Section 52 (2) (a) is as follows:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      169.59,
      665.06,
      535.83,
      706.86
    ],
    "text": "Where the applicant for delivery of possession seeks to evict any person in occupation of a land or a house standing on the land as tenant for a period not exceeding one month who is liable to be evicted by the applicant, such",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.300000190734863,
      11.600000381469727,
      11.642721176147461,
      12.051368713378906,
      12.18452262878418
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      527.62,
      738.98,
      536.32,
      754.45
    ],
    "text": "3",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      158.76,
      72.91,
      525.23,
      116.62
    ],
    "text": "application shall be made by petition to which such person in occupation shall be made respondent, setting out the material facts entitling the applicant to such order.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.85325813293457,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      88.02,
      135.06,
      525.77,
      150.94
    ],
    "text": "In this case admittedly the petitioner was in occupation of the land claiming tenancy",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.474531173706055
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      88.3,
      155.94,
      525.87,
      171.82
    ],
    "text": "rights. The substituted plaintiff, without disclosing that the petitioner was in occupation",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      88.44,
      176.58,
      526.18,
      192.45
    ],
    "text": "of this land, had obtained a writ and got the petitioner evicted. The petitioner after having",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      88.77,
      197.23,
      526.78,
      213.1
    ],
    "text": "made an application to court was placed back in possession. Thereafter the court inquired",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      89.18,
      217.86,
      526.62,
      233.73
    ],
    "text": "in to the petitioner's right to remain in possession. For this purpose the substituted",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.790092468261719,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      89.07,
      238.49,
      526.89,
      254.37
    ],
    "text": "plaintiff filed objections. It is only after this inquiry that the learned Judge made order on",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      89.45,
      258.91,
      449.52,
      274.78
    ],
    "text": "26.1.2006. This order appears to have been made under section 52 (2) (b).",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.880383491516113,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      89.73,
      300.42,
      527.31,
      316.29
    ],
    "text": "At this inquiry what the court had to determine was whether the petitioner had entered in",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      90.22,
      321.05,
      528.61,
      336.93
    ],
    "text": "to occupation prior to the date of the final decree and to determine whether the petitioner",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.474531173706055
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      90.63,
      341.71,
      528.28,
      357.58
    ],
    "text": "is entitled to continue in occupation. Under this section one is entitled to continue in",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      90.61,
      362.58,
      528.52,
      378.45
    ],
    "text": "occupation in the event such person is a tenant for a period not exceeding one month and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      90.73,
      383.21,
      398.08,
      399.09
    ],
    "text": "the lease is in respect of a house. The sub section is as follows:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.804718971252441,
      11.899999618530273,
      12.606525421142578
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      163.4,
      424.75,
      530.21,
      523.41
    ],
    "text": "52 (2) (b): After hearing the respondent, if the court shall determine that the respondent having entered into occupation prior to the date of such final decree .... .is entitled to continue in occupation of the said house as tenant under the applicant as landlord, the court shall dismiss the application; otherwise it shall grant the application and direct that an order for delivery of possession of the said house and land to the applicant do issue (emphasis added).",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.880383491516113,
      11.899999618530273,
      11.909945487976074,
      12.0,
      12.08142375946045,
      12.10940170288086,
      12.11633586883545,
      12.250926971435547,
      12.257389068603516,
      12.34107494354248,
      12.46011734008789,
      12.474531173706055
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      92.86,
      548.34,
      530.45,
      564.22
    ],
    "text": "Under this sub section there is no reference to a land separate from the house. From the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.790092468261719,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.09,
      568.74,
      531.02,
      584.61
    ],
    "text": "material placed before court there is no evidence of occupation of a house. The Rent Act",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574,
      12.474531173706055
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.35,
      589.37,
      531.28,
      605.25
    ],
    "text": "refers to \"premises\". Section 2 (4) of the Rent Act states thus \" .... the provisions of this",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.017717361450195,
      12.206210136413574,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.34,
      610.03,
      531.52,
      625.9
    ],
    "text": "Act shall apply to all premises other than .... \". Section 48 interprets \"premises\" to mean",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.888744354248047,
      11.899999618530273,
      11.909945487976074
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      630.9,
      531.69,
      646.78
    ],
    "text": "any building or part of a building together with the land appertaining thereto; The Rent",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      94.09,
      651.53,
      531.72,
      667.41
    ],
    "text": "Act does not apply to leases in respect of bare land (Jayasiriwardena vs. Piyaratne (2004)",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      95.35,
      672.43,
      373.69,
      688.3
    ],
    "text": "1 Sri L.R. 37, Madanayake vs. Senaratne 75 N.L.R. 349).",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.55983829498291,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      524.36,
      740.89,
      533.28,
      755.59
    ],
    "text": "4",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.699999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      87.26,
      73.15,
      524.99,
      89.02
    ],
    "text": "The learned counsel for the substituted plaintiff submitted that what was let was a bare",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      87.99,
      93.78,
      524.66,
      109.66
    ],
    "text": "land and the lessee had put up a structure only of a semi permanent nature and had to",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      87.83,
      114.66,
      525.31,
      130.54
    ],
    "text": "remove the structures so erected at the expiry of the period. The learned counsel",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      88.15,
      135.29,
      295.01,
      151.17
    ],
    "text": "submitted that the premises is not a house.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      88.73,
      176.59,
      525.82,
      192.46
    ],
    "text": "In Jayawardene vs. Bandaranayake (1998) 3 Sri L.R. 72 Ranaraja J held that a lease is",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.804718971252441,
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      88.91,
      197.22,
      479.61,
      213.09
    ],
    "text": "formed by consent or agreement of the parties on three essential points, namely:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      116.73,
      238.27,
      311.84,
      254.14
    ],
    "text": "1. Object of the contract to let and hire",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.53809642791748,
      11.899999618530273,
      12.206210136413574
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      116.1,
      258.9,
      227.89,
      274.78
    ],
    "text": "2. Ascertain property",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      116.51,
      279.29,
      188.85,
      295.16
    ],
    "text": "3. Fixed rent.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      89.95,
      321.06,
      527.6,
      336.94
    ],
    "text": "Dr. Ranaraja J held that just because there are buildings on a land, if the aforesaid three",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.46011734008789
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      90.63,
      341.94,
      528.06,
      357.82
    ],
    "text": "ingredients are not satisfied there cannot be a contract of tenancy for a building, when",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      90.61,
      362.57,
      528.25,
      378.45
    ],
    "text": "originally the contract was for the letting of a bare land. Dissanayake J in Jayasiriwardene",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273,
      12.34107494354248
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      90.94,
      383.46,
      528.16,
      399.33
    ],
    "text": "vs. Piyaratne (supra) held (pg 45) if the building belonged to the tenant it would not be",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.817161560058594,
      11.899999618530273,
      12.46011734008789
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      90.98,
      404.11,
      528.44,
      419.98
    ],
    "text": "possible to enforce certain rights and duties under the Rent Act and will result in the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      91.31,
      424.74,
      214.51,
      440.61
    ],
    "text": "following consequences:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.899999618530273
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      109.61,
      466.27,
      531.75,
      702.46
    ],
    "text": "1. Under section 22 a landlord would not be able to seek to retake possession of a building that was constructed by the tenant on reasonable requirement. 2. A landlord will not be able to effect repairs to the building as it does not belong to him. 3. If the tenant damages the building the landlord cannot complain as the tenant is the owner of the building. 4. The landlord cannot be made liable for withholding amenities as the building belongs to the tenant. 5. The landlord cannot be made liable if the building collapses due to faulty construction. 6. If on the landlord obtaining a decree on reasonable requirement if the tenant demolishes the house and takes away the material, the landlord will be without a remedy. 7. It would not be possible for anyone to take on rent one's own house and make the owner of the land liable because one cannot lease to himself his own bUilding. 8. If the building was constructed by the tenant and if he causes damage or deterioration to the property, the tenant cannot be evicted by the landlord for",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.146814346313477,
      11.505511283874512,
      11.586315155029297,
      11.594016075134277,
      11.60596752166748,
      11.7592191696167,
      11.789335250854492,
      11.81091594696045,
      11.859580993652344,
      11.899999618530273,
      12.081317901611328,
      12.206210136413574,
      12.27523422241211,
      12.280807495117188,
      12.439998626708984,
      12.46011734008789,
      12.474531173706055
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      523.52,
      741.45,
      532.0,
      756.53
    ],
    "text": "5",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.300000190734863
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      108.35,
      74.35,
      527.42,
      159.81
    ],
    "text": "causing damage or deterioration to the property as he is not the owner of the bUilding. 9. If the building that was constructed by the tenant is sublet the landlord cannot evict him as the landlord has no control over the building. 10. If the building was constructed by the tenant, the landlord cannot ask for vacant possession as the tenant is entitled to remove the structure.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.686432838439941,
      11.794784545898438,
      11.81434154510498,
      11.899999618530273,
      12.108227729797363,
      12.27523422241211,
      12.34107494354248
